# DTF tier manifest: conda-shard-native-search  (artifact-keeper#5432)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single.
#
# THE BUG (1.12.0 pre-release main; the 1.11.x line serves the same records)
# #5432  every record in a CEP-16 shard carried `fn`, although the shard's
#        `packages` / `packages.conda` map already keys the record by its
#        filename. conda 26.7 reads shards by default (repodata_use_shards)
#        and passes the key as `fn` when it builds a PackageRecord, so
#        `conda search` against a hosted or virtual channel failed with
#        "PackageRecord() got multiple values for keyword argument 'fn'".
#
# THE FIX (artifact-keeper#5432's PR)
#        shard records omit `fn` and keep every other field; migration 343
#        rebuilds shards stored by an older writer.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   PUT  /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}  (fixtures/conda/build.sh)
#   GET  /conda/{repo}/noarch/repodata_shards.msgpack.zst, shards/{sha}.msgpack.zst
#        decoded by conda-sharded-remote-virtual/fixtures/cep16.py
#   a REAL conda 26.7 client (docker.io/condaforge/miniforge3:26.7.2-0,
#     `conda search`) behind conda-jlap-incremental/fixtures/logproxy.py in
#     the backend's network namespace
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1): see oracle.sh's header.
COVERS="5432"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
